  "body": "What happens: `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` (on main) and `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` (PR #626) set `sCss` from a `SurfaceSpeed` PARAM and never reset it at a section's end. If one operation states a surface speed and a later one does not, the later one still posts `G96 ... S<css>` with the machine-max `D` cap instead of its own `G97 S<rpm>`. A drilling op on centre (X0) under a stale G96 runs at the cap: the machine's maximum rpm.\n\nToday it is latent: no app code path writes `PARAM SurfaceSpeed`; only the lathe post tests do. It becomes live the moment constant surface speed is wired into the lathe operations.\n\nExpected: each section states its own spindle mode. Reset `sCss = 0` in `endPreamble()` (next to `spinRev = false`) in both posts, and pin it with a two-section stream: a CSS turning section, then a drilling section with no SurfaceSpeed, posting `G97 S<rpm>`.\n\nEffort: high under the safety floor (it changes posted G-code), though the change is two lines plus a test.\n\nDone means: both lathe posts post G97 for a section that states no surface speed after one that did, pinned by a lathe post test in each.\n\nFound while reviewing #626.\n",
